Z||000003||fropuff||11-06-2001||07:22 PM||||Well, it's for the guy that came through the parking lot and ripped the rear end of my Fiero off.  So I did have a reason.  He had no license, a horse-sh*t story, etc.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChopTop||11-06-2001||07:56 PM||||Did you sue him or his insurance company?  Winning the money is one thing, trying to get the money is another when you sue an individual.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||11-06-2001||08:08 PM||||Ya chop, I know what you mean. I dont think thats right either. If you win a court case, I think the court should 'MAKE' them pay or go to jail myself. If you do win, here anyway, you have to file a judgement against them to attach their paycheck or take owned property to get your winnings. So if he dont pay up, you have to take the sherrif with you to confiscate stuff. I hope it works out for you, I hate lowlifes that wont pay up when they screw your car up. Its happened to me too. A guy ran into my Mercedes in a parking lot in front of 100 witnesses, and I never saw a dime. My insurance covered it, but I had to pay the deductible.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fropuff||11-25-2001||07:33 PM||||I'm sure you guys forgot about it and care no longer, but I thought I'd tell you anyway.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I guess the guy has until December 5th to appeal his case.  If he doesn't, I get to collect my settlement.  After December 5th, we send the court papers to his insurance company, to let them know that we won.  AND, either he pays, or his insurance does.  We called the MN state insurance commissioner, and she said that the insurance company will have to pay no matter what, as they did not follow procedure.  I guess they need to ask ME what happened too and not just believe the other guy.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  So I'll have to wait until December 5th and see.  Thanks for all the help though.||||reg||1
